\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises early after  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  reserves jump.  \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2003\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The rupee          rose sharply\par in early deals on Monday, drawing support from a jump in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and a subdued dollar overseas,\par dealers said.\par     At 9:15 a.m. (0335 GMT), the rupee was quoted at\par 45.7350/7450 per dollar, up from the previous close\par 45.8200/8300. It ended up 0.15 percent last week.\par     Data released on the weekend showed India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves leapt $1.11 billion in the week to September\par 5 to a record $87.365 billion on the back of surging foreign\par investment inflows into local shares.\par     The rise represents an inflow of $17.07 billion in 2003,\par with weekly accretions averaging $488 million. Foreign funds\par have pumped in nearly $2.7 billion into Indian shares so far\par this year, compared to $740 million in 2002.\par     Traders said sentiment was also bolstered by news the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's outstanding net forward purchases at the end of\par July totalled $4.549 billion, compared with $3.866 billion in\par the previous month.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The forward contracts would have further gone up in August,\par enabling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet a redemption of Resurgent\par India Bonds of $5.5 billion on October 1 smoothly, traders\par said.\par     Traders said bunched weekend inflows would also push the\par rupee up, but many expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par curb rises.\par     Media reports that Reliance Industries Ltd, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's largest\par petrochemical producer, had got government approval to raise\par $750 million abroad would improve the outlook for the rupee in\par the near term, traders said. Company officials declined comment\par on the report.\par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                             MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    9:15 a.m.    Previous close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)   yet to open    4,305.91\par     Indian rupee (/$)              45.7350/7450  45.8200/8300\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)     not quoted       5.3246\par     Call money (%)                  4.40/4.50      4.40/50\par     6-mth annualised fwd premium (%) yet to open      1.31\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030915dz9f0015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
