\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee ends up for 3rd day, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2003\par 13:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, July 3 (Reuters) - The rupee appreciated for a\par third day on Thursday but gains were muted on dollar purchases\par by state-run banks acting on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par traders said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           ended at 46.40/41 to a dollar,\par firming slightly from its previous close of 46.4150/4250. It\par has gained 3.41 percent in 2003, inching closer to a near\par 29-month high of 46.395/405 at which it ended last week.\par  \par     "The market turned cautious and relatively quiet" after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a foreign bank dealer said.\par     Traders said the rupee was dealt in a very narrow band of\par 46.42 to 46.40, compared with the previous session when it had\par swung between 46.48 and 46.4150.\par     Rupee premiums on forward dollars rose across the curve as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  state-run banks transacted sell-buy swaps to ensure that the \par \par \uc2  dollars they were buying in the spot market did not flood the \par \par \uc2  money market with more rupee funds. \par \par \uc2  Traders said foreign banks also paid forward premiums on \par \par \uc2  behalf of their foreign fund clients to hedge their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  exposures. \par \par \uc2  Growing foreign fund inflows into the local equity and debt \par \par \uc2  markets have been a key driver in the rupee's rise against the \par \par \uc2  greenback in recent months. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The annualised six-month benchmark premium ended 11 basis\par points higher at 2.86 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                     4:05 p.m.      Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)    3,640.94*\par 3,601.39\par     Indian rupee (/$)               46.40/41*\par 46.4150/4250\par     9.81 percent 2013 bond (%)         5.7193\par 5.7201\par     Call money (%)                 4.75/5.00*\par 4.75/5.00\par     6-mth annualised fwd premium (%)    2.86*\par 2.75\par     * - closes\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par     For a speed guide to Reuters treasury coverage,.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030703dz7300li1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
