\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee stuck a notch firmer, dlr fwds rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2003\par 07:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, July 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee remained stuck\par at slightly firmer levels by Thursday mid-morning as anxiety\par about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  muted dollar sales, traders\par said.\par     Rupee premiums on forward dollars rose in early deals as\par expatriate investors in local foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits opted\par to hedge their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk.\par     At 11:00 a.m., the rupee          was at 46.4050/4150 per\par dollar, up from its previous close of 46.4150/4250, but still\par off its early peak of 46.40, hit before some short-covering by\par banks pushed it back a little.\par     "Dollar sellers are wary now after having seen the RBI's\par (Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) determination to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  whenever\par they felt the rupee was rising too much and so the market is in\par a wait and watch mode," a chief dealer at a foreign bank said.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has pinned the rupee down in the past\par three sessions in a sustained manner.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Forward premiums across maturities, with the annualised\par six-month benchmark up three basis points at 2.78 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    11:00 a.m.           9:15\par a.m.\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)     3,606.10\par 3,601.39*\par     Indian rupee