\par\par \b \uc2  WEEK AHEAD-Indian bonds seen stable, eye state loans and c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2003\par 07:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, June 8 (Reuters) - Indian government bond yields are expected to hover near record lows this week in a market flush with funds and bolstered by a favourable outlook for domestic inflation, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But yields are unlikely to drop much after hitting record lows last week, since most investors will be on the sidelines ahead of loan sales by state governments, they said. \par \par \uc2  Also, the market would be apprehensive of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if yields dropped too much. \par \par \uc2  "Bonds are likely to trade in a range this week," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist at JP Morgan Chase. "The state loan sale and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statements towards the end of last week will keep investors cautious." \par \par \uc2  Twenty eight state governments will raise a total of 70 billion rupees ($1.46 billion) by selling 10-year loans on June 12 under a debt swap plan. \par \par \uc2  This is the first tranche of borrowings by states under the plan, which seeks to lower their interest burden, for the current fiscal year, to March 2004. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 10-year bond , which struck a record low of 5.7541 percent on Friday, ended the week at 5.7563 percent, down from the preceding week's 5.7963 percent. \par \par \uc2  It has lost has nearly 40 basis points since start of the financial year in April in a rally driven by liquidity that had been boosted partly by robust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows. \par \par \uc2  India's inflation rate measured by wholesale prices fell to 5.65 percent in the 12 months to May 24, compared with 5.90 percent a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  The trend in the inflation rate has been downwards since it hit a two-year high of 6.47 percent in the year to April 12. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say more dips are likely in the next few weeks due to a fall in energy prices. \par \par \uc2  EYES ON \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Traders said they would keenly watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for cues after it said towards the end of last week that it was unlikely to cut the repo rate in the near term until the monsoon and inflation situation become clearer. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said this verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was uncomfortable with falling yields and wanted bond prices to stabilise. \par \par \uc2  Traders have been speculating that a global easing bias could prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower its repo rate, a benchmark for short-term interest rates, from the current five percent. \par \par \uc2  That speculation was stoked further last Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key interest rate by half a point to two percent. \par \par \uc2  Although the Reserve Bank gives more weight to local factors, such as the monsoon and inflation, and does not necessarily follow rate decisions by other central banks, reductions overseas give it more leeway to pursue a soft rate bias, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  "There is considerable uncertainty about the monsoon," said M.R. Madhavan, analyst at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its statements last week is telling the market not to price in a repo rate cut until the picture about the monsoon becomes clearer." \par \par \uc2  The Indian economy, Asia's third-largest, depends heavily on monsoon rains for demand as around 70 percent of the population lives off the land and agriculture makes up a quarter of the economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030608dz68005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
