\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee snaps 3-day rise as cbank buys dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, March 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended weaker on Friday, snapping a three-day rally as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check its rise and its subsidiary bought dollars to make overseas payments, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee  finished at 47.5500/5525 per dollar, down from the day's high of 47.5325 and Thursday's 18-1/2-month closing peak of 47.5400/5425. \par \par \uc2  "There was support at around the 47.56 level from state-run banks," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "That, combined with demand from a public sector finance company repaying some external borrowing, helped push the rupee down slightly." \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though committed to a market-determined exchange rate, often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to check volatility in the rupee, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, which rose 0.24 percent in three sessions to Thursday, has gained nearly one percent since the start of the year. Analysts said it was, however, still undervalued against the dollar on a trade-weighted basis by about 1.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the robust remittances from software exporters and expatriate Indians seeking to convert their weakening dollar assets into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ones were likely to continue next week, helping the rupee gain further. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts said the rupee's weakening on Friday was only a technical correction, with charts signalling a climb up to the next support level for the dollar at 47.36. \par \par \uc2  Rupee premiums on the forward dollar ended lower, helped by the strong outlook for the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark six-month forward ended four basis points lower at an annualised 3.21 percent. It had eased even lower during the day to 3.15 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030328dz3s00lm4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
