\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee seen gaining, cbank and oil prices eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, March 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee , is expected to extend gains on Friday on strong trade inflows, with the range likely to be set by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Oil prices would also be in market focus as crude is India's biggest import, they said. \par \par \uc2  "There is absolutely no demand for dollars right now because of its (dollar's) weakness. Importers are in a wait-and-watch mode while exporters and companies are bringing in their dollars," a trading head at a private bank said. \par \par \uc2  "So unless the RBI (Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee at a certain level by absorbing the dollar inflows or unless oil prices rise appreciably, the rupee should continue to strengthen gradually." \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended Thursday at a fresh 18-= month closing peak of 47.5400/5425 per dollar, after hitting a key psychological level of 47.54. It has now gained 0.24 percent in three sessions. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rupee would have appreciated further but for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases through state-run banks around 47.54. \par \par \uc2  While the RBI has said the exchange rate is set by market forces, traders say it often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check any sharp moves in the rupee in either direction. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they will also be tracking oil prices for clues on rupee direction as India imports around 1.7 million barrels of oil a day. \par \par \uc2  In Asian trade, front-month May crude  had risen 27 cents to $30.64 per barrel on anxieties about a protracted war in Iraq and Nigerian supply disruptions. Prices are however still way below recent 12-year highs of near $40. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rupee was about undervalued by about 1.7 percent against the dollar at close of trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  PREVIOUS CLOSE: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Call money                  : 6.00-6.25 percent\par  Benchmark 10-year bond yield: 6.2808 percent\par  BSE Sensex                  : 3,116.79 points (-0.85\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indicators:\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves (March 14): $73.92 bln (+$178 mln on week)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inflation - wholesale prices (March 8): 5.13 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par M3 Money supply growth (March 7): 15.5 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RBI advances to government (March 14): Nil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Industrial production (Apr '02-Jan '03): 5.5 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Rupee's intra-day low       : 49.08/dlr on May 16, 2002\par  Rupee's closing low         : 49.0450/0550 on June 3, 2002\par  Bank rate                              : 6.25 percent\par  Repo rate                              : 5.00 percent\par  Cash reserve ratio                     : 4.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030328dz3s005pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
