\par\par \b \uc2  Indian IRS end down, track forward dollar premiums. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 12:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Feb 20 (Reuters) - Indian interest rates swaps (IRS) ended lower on Thursday, tailing forward dollar premiums, which edged down due to a firm outlook for the rupee and talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  receiving, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The five-year swap linked to the implied rupee rate benchmark, the Reuters MIFOR , ended at 6.18/25 percent, down from Wednesday's 6.28/38 percent. The MIFOR is derived from rupee-dollar forwards and U.S. overnight rates. \par \par \uc2  But the five-year swap indexed to the overnight fund benchmark (OIS) ended steady at 6.33/38 percent with the outlook for liquidity remained uncertain as huge bond supplies from several Indian states are expected in the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier in the day it will conduct an on-tap sale for 10-year loans issued by 27 states for a targeted 73.25 billion rupees on February 25. \par \par \uc2  This will be followed by more sales for 68.26 billion before March-end. \par \par \uc2  But some traders are of the view that the sales could go through without impacting liquidity much as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to mop up some of the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to absorb \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows to curb a sharp upswing in the rupee and in the process boosts money market liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The rupee , which analysts say is undervalued by nearly three percent on a trade-weighted basis, ended steady at 47.6975/7075 per dollar, off a low of 47.7175 in early deals. \par \par \uc2  Rupee premiums on the forward dollar eased in late trade as talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  receiving prompted some exporters to sell forward dollars in anticipation of further drops. \par \par \uc2  The annualised premium on the six-month dollar closed at 3.62 percent against the previous 3.7 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030220dz2k01dp0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
