\par\par \b \uc2  Indian IRS steady, firm outlook for rupee helps. \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Feb 20 (Reuters) - Indian interest rates swaps were mostly steady on Thursday, with a firm undertone for the rupee offsetting an uncertain liquidity and rate outlook, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The five-year swap indexed to the overnight fund benchmark (OIS)  was at 6.31/41 percent, compared with the previous close of 6.33/43. \par \par \uc2  The five-year swap linked to the implied rupee rate benchmark, the Reuters MIFOR , was quoted at 6.27/37 percent, barely changed from Wednesday's 6.28/38 percent. \par \par \uc2  The MIFOR is derived from rupee-dollar forwards and U.S. overnight rates. \par \par \uc2  "There are concerns about how liquidity will be after the state loan sales," said a dealer in a securities firm. "But with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mopping up dollar inflows, a view is gaining ground that the sales are unlikely to impact fund supplies much." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to absorb \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows to curb a sharp upswing in the rupee and in the process boosts money market liquidity. \par \par \uc2  At 12:20 p.m. (0640 GMT), the rupee , which analysts say is undervalued by nearly three percent on a trade-weighted basis, was quoted at 47.695/705, off a low of 47.7175 in early deals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday that several of India's 28 states would together borrow up to 141.51 billion rupees before the financial year ends on March 31, a move which could squeeze supplies and 