\par\par \b \uc2  Indian call rate rises, checks dip in bond yields. \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2003\par 05:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 17 (Reuters) - India's overnight funds rate jumped on Friday due to huge outflows towards the previous day's open market bond auctions, slowing a fall in bond yields, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But they said investors drew some comfort from a senior central banker's comments that the market would determine the realistic levels of bond yields. \par \par \uc2  Call money  was quoted at 6.00-6.25 percent at 10:00 a.m. (0430 GMT), up from the previous close of 5.25-5.50 percent, with auction outflows of nearly 109 billion denting fund supply. \par \par \uc2  "But this is not detering investors to buy bonds in small quantums at the long end," said a trader at a primary dealer. "They are convinced that the spike (in call money) is temporary and the liquidity situation will improve in a few days." \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 10-year 9.81 percent bond was at 5.9125 percent, down from the previous close 5.9275 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent purchase of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has boosted supplies in India's domestic money market, fuelling a bond market rally and spurring hopes a repo rate cut. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past to mop up excess funds through open market bond sales, a possibility the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor reiterated on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity continues to be under constant watch and that is why we did the open market sales (on Thursday)," RBI Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan told reporters on the sidelines of a management seminar. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to monitor the situation," he replied, when asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider more open market sales. \par \par \uc2  He said monetary authorities were neither comfortable nor uncomfortable with the current bond yield levels. \par \par \uc2  "The market will decide the realistic level of bond yields," he answered, when asked to comment on why yields had fallen despite the open market auctions on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030117dz1h008hm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
