\par\par \b \uc2  WEEK AHEAD-C.bank sale fears to support Indian bond yields. \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2003\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Indian bond yields could ease to fresh life lows this week, but fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell stock should temper any decline, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI (Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is well armoured to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should yields fall too fast," said S. Ananthanarayan, vice president at Kotak Mahindra Capital Co. \par \par \uc2  "I expect a very mild easing, with the 10-year yield falling to 5.97 percent over a week to 10 days. The market will correct itself at every stage in the anxiety of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale." \par \par \uc2  The 10-year yield was 6.0080 percent on Saturday, after hitting a life low of 5.9984 percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Surplus cash from strong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows have pushed bond yields to historic lows, leaving 10-year bonds yielding just half a percentgae point over interbank overnight interest rates. \par \par \uc2  But with banks still holding surplus cash, traders said pressure on bond yields would continue. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , wary with yields at such low levels, is well positioned to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  having added four new bonds to its portfolio after special federal securities worth 200 billion rupees were converted in early January. \par \par \uc2  The key 10-year yield fell a percentage point between the end of October and December and has fallen a further six-basis points in January because of the easy money conditions, benign inflation and fears for the economy after a severe drought. \par \par \uc2  Central bankers have said there were no plans to cut interest rates in the near term, but traders are factoring in a 50-basis-point cut in the key short-term benchmark - the repo rate, which stands at 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  This rate, at which RBI borrows overnight funds from the market, influences the cost of interbank funds and consequently, bond yields. \par \par \uc2  The next monetary policy is to be announced in April. \par \par \uc2  MORE FLATTENING \par \par \uc2  The yield curve has already flattened considerably since the end of October and medium and long end could fall further on the loose liquidity conditions. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the curve would continue to flatten till the repo rate was cut as only then would yields fall at the short end of the curve. \par \par \uc2  The spread between the one-and 10-year bond yields have narrowed to 62 basis points from 124 basis points, while the spreads between the 10-and 15-year bond yields have tightened to 14 basis points from 31. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030112dz1c00a16\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
