\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends firm, ignores dlr's global rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2003\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     BOMBAY, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended stronger\par on Tuesday as healthy dollar inflows helped the unit shrug off\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise overseas.\par     The rupee          closed at 47.9775/47.9825 per dollar, up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  from Monday's 47.9875/9925. It had hit a trough of 48.0175 in \par \par \uc2  the morning after state-run banks bought dollars to check its \par \par \uc2  rise. \par \par \uc2  "There was heavy selling towards the afternoon, including by \par \par \uc2  some corporates, and dollar supplies were abundant," said a \par \par \uc2  trader at a state-run bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders also took heart from a fall in world prices of oil, \par \par \uc2  India's biggest import item, and shrugged off the dollar's \par \par \uc2  overseas rise a day before U.S. President George W. Bush is to \par \par \uc2  unveil an economic stimulus plan expected to be worth up to as \par \par \uc2  much as $670 billion. \par \par \uc2  Oil prices fell after a senior OPEC delegate said major \par \par \uc2  producers were preparing to raise output as soon as possible to \par \par \uc2  cool crude markets, overheated by the threat of war in Iraq and \par \par \uc2  a continuing strike in Venezuela, the world's fifth biggest oil \par \par \uc2  exporter. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \par \par \uc2  dollar in recent weeks in its keenness to protect the country's \par \par \uc2  export competitiveness. The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been aimed at \par \par \uc2  capping the local unit's appreciation at around the 48 level. \par \par \uc2  The rupee rose 0.55 percent in 2002, its first annual gain \par \par \uc2  in more than 10 years, helped by heavy remittances by overseas \par \par \uc2  Indians, exporters and foreign portfolio and direct investors. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves leapt $22.25 billion last year to \par \par \uc2  more than $70 billion as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  absorbed most of the \par \par \uc2  inflows to rein in the rupee. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The forward market moved in step with the spot market, with\par rupee premiums ending slightly lower.\par     The benchmark six-month premium closed at an annualised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3.46 percent against its previous close of 3.47 percent. It was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted even lower at 3.44 percent for most of the day before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some late paying took it up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030107dz1700mjb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
