\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Indian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves vault over $67 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2002\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 14 (Reuters) - Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by a sharp $828 million in the week to December 6, to a new high of $67.753 billion, data from the Reserve Bank of India's Weekly Statistical Supplement showed on Saturday. Analysts said the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were boosted by continuing exporter remittances, coupled with steady dollar purchases by state-run banks on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to temper the rupee's gains. \par \par \uc2  "Since the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, we had expected reserves to rise," said Sanjeet Singh, analyst with ICICI Securities and Finance Company. \par \par \uc2  "But the quantum of the rise is a bit higher than expected and that is probably on account of revaluation of the dollar against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  India's foreign curreny assets, expressed in dollars, include the effect of appreciation or depreciation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Euro, Sterling and Yen. \par \par \uc2  The Euro gained 1.52 percent against the dollar in the week ended December 6. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been checking the rupee's gains since June to maintain the export competitiveness of Indian goods and servces and beef up reserves. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee closed at 48.1675/1775 per dollar on Friday against the previous close of 48.1875/1975. It is up 1.87 percent since hitting a lifetime low of 49.08 per dollar in mid-May, but is still undervalued by two percent on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  Given the country's healthy external finances, as reflected in a small current account surplus in the first quarter of the current year, and favourable interest rate differentials, dollar inflows are likely to gather pace in the next few months, analysts say. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021214dyce00ac9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
