\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends at 2002 high, fwds up on cbank. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2002\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended at a 2002 closing high against the dollar on Wednesday, boosted by robust remittances by exporters and banks going short on the greenback on hopes that more gains were in store for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They added that the rupee was also encouraged by indications that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not making wholehearted attempts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and temper gains. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2   ended at 48.1475/1575 per dollar, up from the previous close of 48.1950/2050, itself a two-week closing high. The last time the rupee finished around this level was on December 26 last year. \par \par \uc2  It has so far gained 1.9 percent from its mid-May life low of 49.08, but is still undervalued by about two percent on a trade-weighted basis due to the latest bout of weakness afflicting the dollar overseas. \par \par \uc2  The unit was undervalued by about one percent last week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "There were attempts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar at every level," a dealer at a foreign bank said. "But the inflows were quite robust." \par \par \uc2  Traders had expected state-run banks, which often act on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to prevent the rupee from rising beyond 48.18 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India has been absorbing a bulk of the dollar supplies in recent months to maintain the export competitiveness of Indian goods and beef up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS TREND UP \par \par \uc2  Despite the firm local unit, rupee premiums on the forward dollar ended firmer on sustained paying (sell-buy swaps) by banks, possibly acting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keen to correct a distortion in short-term rates by sucking out rupee funds. \par \par \uc2  As a result of their persistent paying, the six-month dollar-rupee implied rate  inched up to around the repo rate of 5.50 percent after staying below the overnight funds rate for the past three weeks. \par \par \uc2  The implied rates indicate how much rupee loans can earn in the local money market and are derived from the forward dollar premiums and U.S. interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  Forwards reflect the hedging requirements by importers and the interest rate differentials between the United States and India. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward closed at 3.87 percent, up from previous close of 3.82 percent while the six-months ended at 3.97 percent, higher than the previous close of 3.96 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021211dycb00kor\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
