\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends 3-day rising streak, forwards up. \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2002\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee snapped a three-day rising streak to end weaker on Thursday after dollar bids from state-run banks, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushed it down and prompted some banks to cover short positions. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at 48.2425/2575 per dollar, down from the previous close of 48.2025/2100. At Wednesday's close, the rupee had gained 0.2 percent during the week. \par \par \uc2  It has risen about 1.8 percent since it hit a lifetime low of 49.08 in mid-May but is still undervalued about a percent on a trade-weighted basis, which analysts say is probably prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to maintain the rupee's real effective exchange rate and beef up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Traders said banks were also paying (sell-buy swaps) at the short-end of the forward segment which led to a spike in rupee premiums across the curve. \par \par \uc2  "The banks paid on behalf of some importers and the market is correcting itself," said a trader at a state-run bank. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward ended at at an annualised 3.08 percent up from the previous close of 2.51 percent. The six-month forward closed at 3.66 percent, firmer than the previous 3.57 percent. \par \par \uc2  Low premiums in the past two weeks have kept the one-year implied dollar-rupee rate  below the overnight funds rate, a short-term benchmark in the domestic money market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the paying by the banks was correcting this discrepancy. \par \par \uc2  A lower one-year implied rate means that borrowers can raise short-term dollar funds at a cheaper rate than the overnight domestic money market level. \par \par \uc2  Forwards also reflect the hedging needs of importers and interest rate differences between the United States and India. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021205dyc500muc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
