\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee extends rise, state banks curb gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2002\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended gains on Wednesday afternoon, helped by exporter remittances, although state-run banks, which sometimes act on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , curbed its rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 1:15 p.m., the Indian unit was quoted at 48.5350/5450 against the morning's 48.5525/5625 and Tuesday's six-and-a-half month closing high of 48.56/57. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be allowing a gradual appreciation in the rupee, while slowing a rise," said a dealer at a state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stated objective for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is to maintain stability, which analysts say it does by tempering sharp movements in the rupee and steering it towards its trade-weighted value. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar weakening overseas in recent months, the rupee is estimated to be undervalued by more than four percent in trade-weighted terms. \par \par \uc2  Premiums on the forward dollar eased as exporters sold in the forward market as well to cash in on current levels in the face of a positive outlook for the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The six-month annualised premium was eased to 4.22 percent from the previous 4.28 percent. \par \par \uc2  For earlier reports on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \par \par \uc2  For a speed guide to Reuters treasury cove