\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee steady at open, bias firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, March 18 (Reuters) - The rupee traded steady in thin Monday morning deals with traders saying the incentive to sell dollars remained strong despite likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders also said they expected the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) will continue its vigorous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars through state-run banks to check the rupee's gains. Despite a one percent fall so far in 2002, the rupee is nearly a percent overvalued in real terms. \par \par \uc2  "It's judicious to keep a short or square dollar position," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "There is no reason to expect pressure on the rupee, and the carry may keep rising as the year end approaches." \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 48.71/72 per dollar in early trade, little changed from Friday's close at 48.7050/7150. \par \par \uc2  Call rates continued to be in a higher range around seven percent. They rose last week from steady levels around the 6.5 percent refinance rate on outflows towards tax payments and the pressure of the approaching fiscal year end. \par \par \uc2  Last week's tensions, because of plans by Hindu hardliners to hold a prayer ceremony in Ayodhya, had receded and traders were indifferent to reports of firing across the border between India and Pakistan in Kashmir, saying it was routine. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows to continue, especially regular flows from multinationals hiking their stake in Indian subsidiaries. \par \par \uc2  The latest was UK household products firm Reckitt Benckiser Plc , which last week made an open offer to buy out the remaining 49 percent holding in Reckitt Benckiser (India) . \par \par \uc2  They also expect a spillover of last week's quarterly payments for a television broadcasting firm. \par \par \uc2  For a speed guide to Reuters treasury coverage, \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020318dy3i00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
