\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Indian rupee hits new low, market sees cbank hand. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2002\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee tumbled to a historic low on Tuesday, but caused few flutters among traders who viewed it as another routine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inspired depreciation to adjust an overvaluation. \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit a low of 48.7450 per dollar, erasing last week's intraday trough of 48.6250. The fall took the losses to one percent in 2002 and 4.38 percent since the start of the financial year on April 1. \par \par \uc2  It ended at a new closing low for a second day at 48.6450/6600 against 48.61/62 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "No doubt it is a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -planned move to depreciate the rupee. But they also want a slower pace and maybe felt today's fall was overdone," a dealer with an American bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales by state-run banks that normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) helped the rupee recover partially, but traders said the bout of weakness may continue. \par \par \uc2  Even after Tuesday's drop, the rupee is estimated to be overvalued by more than 2.5 percent on a trade-weighted basis, and analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is constrained to ensure export competitiveness of the rupee to support economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Year-on-year export growth in the first nine months has been almost flat and GDP growth last year was a low four percent. \par \par \uc2  "Every new level being defined has the RBI's tacit approval," said a foreign bank's head of treasury. \par \par \uc2  The current bout of weakness in the rupee was triggered last week by talk of some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deals and heavy payment of overseas dividends by a telecommunications firm. \par \par \uc2  Although state-run banks sold dollars when the rupee hit lows last week, traders felt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be averse to a downward move in the overvalued rupee. \par \par \uc2  "There must be some pressure on the RBI...for export performance to improve they must be having some notional target," said Sanjeet Singh, analyst with ICICI Securities and Finance Corp (I-Sec). \par \par \uc2  "And our comfort is drawn from RBI's comfort," Singh said. \par \par \uc2  SLOWING FUND INFLOWS \par \par \uc2  Foreign direct investment and expatriate flows have been heavy in the past two months, pushing reserves to record highs of more than $49 billion, but portfolio flows have been fickle. \par \par \uc2  Foreign institutional investors (FIIs) invested just over $137 million in Indian stocks and bonds in January, sharply lower than the $908 million in the same month last year. \par \par \uc2  "...the lack of supply from the FII front is showing up now as the nationalised demand remains at consistent levels," Standard Chartered Bank said in a market commentary. \par \par \uc2  BONDS UNPERTURBED \par \par \uc2  The rupee's fall halted a sharp rally in government bonds, but traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness was not a big concern. \par \par \uc2  The possibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversing a softening interest rate policy to defend the rupee was virtually ruled out given the sluggish demand and languishing industrial sector. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 10-year yield, at 7.5623 percent, was off an early low of 7.5490 percent but is down some 35 basis points since January. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020205dy2500ezj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
