\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Indian Rupee Sells Off As Border Tension Increases \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nivedita Prabhu \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2002\par 15:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY -(Dow Jones)- The Indian rupee closed at an all time low against the dollar for the fourth successive day Friday after the army chief spoke of a worsening crisis on the border with Pakistan. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, which was already weakening early Friday, driven down by demand for dollars from state-run banks, fell further when Army Chief S. Padmanabhan described the situation on the border as "serious" after the recent troop build-up by both India and Pakistan. \par \par \uc2  The rupee closed at INR48.4150 to the dollar, down from its previous close of INR48.36. The record intraday low is INR48.44 Sept. 17, a week after the terrorists attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not taking any measures to stop the fall, dealers expect the rupee to remain under pressure. \par \par \uc2  On Monday it is expected to trade in a INR48.35-45 range and touch INR48.50 by the end of January. \par \par \uc2  The deployment of troops along the border follows an attack on the Indian Parliament on Dec. 13 by militants whom India says were based in Pakistan. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been steadily weakening nearly every day of the current week, largely driven down by state-run banks buying dollars at a steady pace, possibly to pay for oil and defense imports. \par \par \uc2  "After the army chief's remarks, no one wanted to remain short on the dollar," said K. Jayaram, Vice President, \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Credit Lyonnais, who noted that some importers may have wanted to cover their positions ahead of any developments over the weekend. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Correction Overdue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupee's fall in reaction to the Army Chief's press conference\par wasn't sharp, however, dealers noted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market had been expecting the rupee to continue to weaken Friday\par after closing at a record low Thursday following dollar purchases by\par state-run banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The expectation was based on the assumption that the Reserve Bank\par would like the rupee to weaken as it was overvalued on a trade-related\par basis, specially after the recent fall of the yen against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't directly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. However it operates in the market through state-owned\par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Some correction has ensued from state-run banks buying dollars but\par there is still room for more," Jayaram added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said that the Reserve Bank is allowing the rupee to weaken\par steadily. "Ever since the beginning of January, a lot of the downward\par move of the rupee seems to have been driven by the Reserve Bank of\par India," said Rajesh Gosain, Senior Dealer, Centurion Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Gosain felt that it wasn't necessary to link the RBI's role in\par engineering a weaker rupee to the fall in the yen. "There is no pressure\par in the rupee from a weaker yen, " he said. "There are other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par such as the euro and the dollar which are more important," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However market analysts have been expecting the RBI to prefer a weaker\par rupee to help India's export competitiveness. The government recently\par revised the export growth target to 3% from 12% as the global economy\par slowed down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Nivedita Prabhu, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22\par 2884211;nivedita.prabhu@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020111dy1b000to\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
