\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee falls prey to too much stability. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 11:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee has once again bucked the regional trend to hit new troughs against the dollar, and analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long period of stability, besides new uncertainties, is a factor driving it lower. \par \par \uc2  In Wednesday morning deals, the rupee traded a 47.92-47.96 range, steadier than it has been in nearly a week and down about 1.7 percent this month. \par \par \uc2  A major part of those losses came after September 11, the day aerial attacks destroyed the World Trade Center in New York, paralysing the U.S. and world financial markets. \par \par \uc2  During the week, major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the euro and Japanese yen have gained sharply against the dollar, prompting Japanese authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while regionals have firmed or been stable. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rupee had diverged from this trend as it had started sliding a week before the U.S. attacks, after two months of stability and a decline of just a percent until end-August. \par \par \uc2  That was bound to accelerate as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit stop-losses and unnerved importers as it fell, they said. \par \par \uc2  Many believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had encouraged the initial move to correct an over-valuation in trade-weighted terms, although it probably \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  later to check a runaway drop. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has traditionally been prone to sudden, rapid bouts of depreciation after months of stability. At its lifetime low of 48.43 hit on Monday, it was down just 3.65 percent this year. \par \par \uc2  "Technical factors are driving the rupee lower. It had been overvalued and it had to drop substantially after a long period of stability," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with an American bank, said. \par \par \uc2  Others blamed market controls for the rupee's runaway slide. \par \par \uc2  Speculative trade in the rupee, which is only partially convertible on the capital account, is banned and the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee is very susceptible to event risk. The fear psychosis in Indian markets is such that any bad news causes all the nervous shorts to cover," said V. Ravikumar, treasury head at private sector Vysya Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Other markets are far more rational." \par \par \uc2  UNCERTAINTIES MOUNT \par \par \uc2  Despite the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market being relatively sheltered, analysts said the U.S. attacks had raised risks for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This is a natural reaction to uncertainty. There are a larger number of unknowns now," said Siddharth Mathur, economist with JP Morgan in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  Strong foreign portfolio investments totalling $2.7 billion supported the rupee through the first eight months of 2001, helping it weather political scandals, a stock market crisis and downgrades by international rating firms. \par \par \uc2  The RBI added $10 billion to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are in excess of $45 billion, in the 12 months to August. \par \par \uc2  But analysts say even those flows are now at risk. \par \par \uc2  And, they said, it was immaterial whether India supports the United States in the retaliation being planned against Afghanistan, which is sheltering Saudi-born dissident Osama bin Laden, the prime suspect in last week's attacks on Washington and New York. \par \par \uc2  It is willy-nilly going to bear the brunt of mounting tension in the immediate neighbourhood. \par \par \uc2  "Unfortunately we are grouped with other South Asian nations, and hence more vulnerable to any fallouts of these U.S. attacks," said a spot rupee trader with a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Economists said investors scaling back exposures to the United States may choose eastern countries like Singapore and Indonesia over India, both for their open markets and location. \par \par \uc2  RISK FACTOR \par \par \uc2  Merrill Lynch said it favoured countries with large domestic economies, but ranked India after China and Australia because its "geographical proximity to Afghanistan could be a risk factor". \par \par \uc2  The trade account could be hit on both sides. Any rise in oil prices will be a big blow for the country, which imports a large part of its crude oil needs. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan's Mathur said another risk comes from further deceleration in consumer spending in the United States, which besides being the market for a fifth of India's exports is also the biggest buyer of the country's consumer goods. \par \par \uc2  The key Bombay share index plunged close to an eight-year low on Monday, making the domestic market among the worst performing in Asia this year, although news on Tuesday of government moves to boost trading helped shares partly rebound. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j00bw4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
