\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee breathes easier,shares in relief rally. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 18 (Reuters) - India's battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got some respite on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soothed sentiment, while shares saw a relief recovery after Wall Street performed within expectations on reopening for trade. \par \par \uc2  At 11:20 a.m. (0550 GMT), the rupee was quoted at 47.91/95 per dollar - weaker than Monday's record closing low of 47.83/88 but well off its lifetime trough of 48.43, hit on the same day. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Bombay exchange index was up 4.37 percent at 2,798.04 points, after diving 15 percent since the killer attacks on the U.S. a week ago. \par \par \uc2  In comparison, the Dow Jones index fell only 7.13 percent on Monday, when it resumed after a four-day shut down. \par \par \uc2  But traders said sentiment remained cautious, given that the domestic economy was grappling with a two-year slowdown and there were growing fears of a global recession. \par \par \uc2  Fears over the possible fallout from expected U.S. reprisals against Afghanistan, which is sheltering Osama bin Laden, the prime suspect in the airborne attacks, also weighed on the market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SUPPORT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt markets were heartened by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has offered to purchase four bonds on Tuesday to provide market liquidity. \par \par \uc2  On Monday it was believed to have sold dollars through state-run banks after the rupee hit record lows for the seventh straight session. \par \par \uc2  "First, they (RBI) made some strong statements on Saturday, then they followed it up with firm action," said the treasury head at a private bank. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like they will not defend any levels but they are obviously not going to allow sharp movements either," he said. \par \par \uc2  At its lowest on Monday, the rupee had lost 1.28 percent on the day, extending its losses for this month to 2.68 percent. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, it has weakened 3.65 percent against the dollar, compared with an average annual depreciation of five to six percent in recent years. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspect its latest spell of weakness, which started before the attacks in the United States, was initially with the RBI's blessings and meant to correct an overvaluation in trade-weighted terms against major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  It is now estimated to be undervalued by about one percent. \par \par \uc2  "With the dollar weakening and oil prices off highs immediately after the attacks, there is no immediate reason for any further rupee weakness," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "We only have to make sure there is no negative trigger to sentiment," he said. \par \par \uc2  SHARES FIRM ON REGIONALS \par \par \uc2  Share prices took comfort from regional markets which were mostly firm in early trading. \par \par \uc2  "The overnight Fed rate cut and firm strong regionals have held the market," said Chetan Kapoor at KJMC Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  Winners outpaced losers 505 to 162 on the Bombay exchange but traders said underlying sentiment was shaky and investors were unwilling to take on bigger positions. \par \par \uc2  The uptrend was led by index-heavyweight Reliance Industries , the India's largest petrochemicals maker, which jumped 4.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  Hindustan Lever Ltd , the biggest consumer goods maker, rose 4.7 percent and Infosys Technologies , the country's second-biggest software exporter, rose 5.6 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010918dx9i00cd3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
