\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee hits new low, foreign banks buy dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2001\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The rupee          hit a new\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low of 47.31 in Monday afternoon deals, driven by a sudden bout\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  of heavy dollar purchases by some large foreign banks. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said state-run banks sold dollars at that level, \par \par \uc2  believed to be at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but these \par \par \uc2  supplies were quickly mopped up by the market. \par \par \uc2      At 0710 GMT, the rupee was quoted at 47.2975/3075 per \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2      It had weakened gradually last week, ending Friday at a new \par \par \uc2  low of 47.2575/2700 on mismatches in dollar flows, coupled with \par \par \uc2  concerns over declining foreign fund inflows and a wobbly stock \par \par \uc2  market. It fell 0.3 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was not clear if Monday's falls were on \par \par \uc2  account of dollar purchases by foreign funds, although banks \par \par \uc2  offering custodial services to foreign funds were bidding for \par \par \uc2  the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Latest data from the capital market regulator showed \par \par \uc2  foreign funds were net sellers of shares and bonds worth $28.2 \par \par \uc2  million in the first four working days of September. \par \par \uc2  Foreign fund investments have supported the rupee this \par \par \uc2  year, but their net purchases in shares and bonds dropped to \par \par \uc2  $83 million in August, their lowest monthly investment in 2001. \par \par \uc2      Their net investments total $2.67 billion so far this year \par \par \uc2  against $1.56 billion for the whole of 2000. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) may temper \par \par \uc2  sharp falls by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks, but may not \par \par \uc2  be averse to let the rupee weaken slightly to adjust for a long \par \par \uc2  period of near static trade. \par \par \uc2  The rupee is currently around one percent overvalued in \par \par \uc2  real terms. Despite the fall to its record low, the rupee is \par \par \uc2  only around 1.3 percent weaker against the dollar than at the \par \par \uc2  start of 2001. \par \par \uc2  Forwards were up but just marginally so in Monday's deals, \par \par \uc2  with the sharp drop in rates in the United States keeping \par \par \uc2  bidders at bay. \par \par \uc2      Six-month premiums were around 3-4 basis points higher than \par \par \uc2  Friday's close of 4.71 percent. \par \par \uc2      For a speed guide to Reuters treasury coverage, double \par \par \uc2  click on , , . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010910dx9a00fx4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
