\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Indian markets discount downgrades, but analysts wary. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2001\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Indian financial markets were steady on Thursday despite the move by Moody's Investors Service to follow its ratings agency peer Standard & Poor's (S&P) in downgrading the country's rating outlook. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the downgrades held little new downside risk for markets which have already been rattled this year by a series of political and financial sector scandals and an economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2  They noted that the Indian economy did not rely heavily on foreign borrowings, the one source of capital most likely to react immediately to revisions in ratings. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended at 47.1225/1300 per dollar, off 47.14 hit in some morning deals and compared with Wednesday's close of 47.11/12. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Bombay exchange share index ended up 0.52 percent at 3,319.61 points. \par \par \uc2  The 10-year bond was traded at 114.30 rupees in evening trade, compared with 114.14 the previous day. This bond was traded at 113.70 rupees on Tuesday evening before the two downgrades were announced. \par \par \uc2  Late on Wednesday, Moody's said it was lowering the outlook for India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to stable from positive and that on domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to negative from positive, citing the government's failure to implement macroeconomic reforms. \par \par \uc2  The move came a day after S&P downgraded India's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating and outlook, citing high budget deficits and rising domestic debt. \par \par \uc2  Both agencies have a junk bond rating on India. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the reasons cited by the two agencies were not new and had been discounted by local markets, which have been shaken over the past six months by a series of political and financial sector scandals. \par \par \uc2  RBI MAY HAVE BEEN IN MARKET \par \par \uc2  Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond traders suspected that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also helped ensure market stability. \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) Governor Bimal Jalan told reporters in New Delhi that there was no need for an immediate interest rate cut but added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make one if the economy required such a move. \par \par \uc2  Most bond traders took heart from Jalan's comments, interpreting them as an indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue with an easy money policy. \par \par \uc2  Some saw the comments as an attempt to talk up a market which while stable, appeared to be nervous about future direction. \par \par \uc2  "Bonds are moving up, but Jalan's comments seem to be some attempt to undo negative (sentiment)," said a dealer at a private bank. Jalan made similar comments on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Besides the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars through state-run banks on Wednesday to shore up the rupee when it slipped to 47.185 per dollar in thin early deals - within striking distance of its lifetime low of 47.21 on July 3. \par \par \uc2  Share prices were stable as traders saw little impact on foreign fund inflows from the rating revisions. \par \par \uc2  "It will make no difference to equity flows," said the chief investment officer at a domestic mutual fund. \par \par \uc2  "For the foreign investor India is not a macro story. They have always adopted a bottom up investment strategy, the stock picking approach," he said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have poured money into Indian stocks despite a steep fall in share prices this year, with the market rocked by broker payment defaults, liquidity problems on stock exchanges and a crisis at the country's largest mutual fund. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Bombay exchange index has lost nearly 17 percent since January. Yet net investments by foreign funds in shares total some $2.5 billion so far this year against $1.53 billion in the whole of last year. \par \par \uc2  ANALYSTS WARY \par \par \uc2  But analysts were cautious, saying that while the downgrades would not result in a pullout by foreign funds from India, it would scare off potential investors in the short term and add to the negative sentiment afflicting investors. \par \par \uc2  The economy has slowed for two years in a row, with no signs of an immediate turnaround. \par \par \uc2  The government has spent most of its time fighting off opposition allegations of involvements in scandals - weakening its ability to push through key reforms. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010809dx8900fbe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
