\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee - Factors to watch - August 8. \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2001\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Aug 8 (Reuters) - The rupee          is expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open weak on Wednesday reacting to Standard & Poor's downgrade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  of India's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating and outlook. \par \par \uc2      - The rupee ended little changed at 47.1125/1200 per dollar \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday, before the S&P announcement. \par \par \uc2      - S&P on Tuesday lowered India's long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  sovereign credit rating to BBB-minus from BBB. \par \par \uc2      - It affirmed its BB long-term and single B short-term \par \par \uc2  foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit and A-3 short-term local \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit ratings on the country. The outlook \par \par \uc2  for both long-term ratings was revised to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2      - The rating agency said the downgrade reflects unchecked \par \par \uc2  budget deficits and rising domestic indebtedness. \par \par \uc2      - Dealers said the immediate reaction will see importers \par \par \uc2  hedge some payables and banks build up long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      - The rupee's stability so far has been due to sluggish \par \par \uc2  import demand for dollars caused by an industrial slowdown, \par \par \uc2  strong capital inflows and the expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  will keep a tight leash on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  - "There is some element of enquiry among corporate \par \par \uc2  clients. People will wait till tomorrow to take a call on the \par \par \uc2  rupee," said S. Rosha, head of corporate treasury sales at \par \par \uc2  HSBC. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers expect the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks if the rupee falls to \par \par \uc2  47.15-47.20. \par \par \uc2  - Foreign funds have been dollar buyers in recent sessions \par \par \uc2  and sustained bids from them could put more pressure on the \par \par \uc2  rupee, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  - Foreign fund investments in Indian shares and bonds had \par \par \uc2  slowed to a trickle. So far in August their net purchases of \par \par \uc2  Indian assets was $27.9 million. Their net purchases had fallen \par \par \uc2  in July to $92 million, the lowest so far in 2001. \par \par \uc2  - The rupee's weakness and rise in bond yields will also \par \par \uc2  keep forwards bid. The six-month forward ended Tuesday at 4.72 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2     . \par \par \uc2      Previous closing rates: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates            : 6.85-6.95 percent\par     BSE 30-share Index          : 3,319.67 points (-0.31 pct)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indicators:\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves (July 27): $43.682 bln (+$78 mln for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Inflation - wholesale prices (July 21) : 4.96 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     M3 Money supply growth (June 29)      : 16.8 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Industrial production (April-May)     : 2.6 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Rupee's intra-day low     : 47.21/dlr on July 3, 2001\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For a speed guide to Reuters treasury coverage, double\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par click on , , .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00