\par\par \b \uc2  India's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves rise to record $42.7 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2001\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, April 21 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $42.722 billion in the week to April 12, up $33 million over the previous week, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rise in reserves was despite the central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (RBI) suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to defend the falling rupee during that week. \par \par \uc2  The rupee began sliding on April 10 after weeks of steady trade, dragged by a plunging stock market and fears foreign investment flows would fall. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's fall was exacerbated by the market view that the rupee was overvalued against its trade-weighted index following recent falls in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The increase in reserves is hardly anything. It could be on account of revaluation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket, or interest on investments, or the foreign fund inflows that we have seen," M.R. Madhavan, head of research at Bank of America, said. \par \par \uc2  India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets expressed in dollar terms include the effect of appreciation or depreciation of non-U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the euro, sterling and yen, held in reserves. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have been net buyers of $318.3 million in Indian markets in April so far. \par \par \uc2  The rupee fell more than one percent to an all-time low of 47.10 on April 17 before recovering on a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's remarks the market might have been overestimating the rupee's overvaluation. \par \par \uc2  It ended Friday at 46.8000/8150 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  There has been an almost continual rise in reserves since the end of 2000, helped by foreign capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Besides the $5.5 billion raised from expatriate Indians through the Millennium Deposit Scheme last November, portfolio inflows in 2001 have been heavy, totalling a net of over $2 billion so far. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rupee still has room to depreciate. \par \par \uc2  "On a trade-weighted basis, the rupee is still overvalued by close to three percent," JP Morgan Securities said in a recent report. \par \par \uc2  "A further one percent correction in the rupee value appears likely in the near term and the RBI would be willing to tolerate this," it said. \par \par \uc2  In its monetary policy for 2001/02 released on Thursday, the RBI estimated GDP growth this financial year at 6.0-6.5 percent despite the uncertain industrial outlook. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left unchanged the bank rate, which it has cut by 100 basis points since February, but indicated a bias for softer rates and assured markets it would provide the needed liquidity. \par \par \uc2  It cut the ceiling on the rates banks can offer on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expatriate deposits to LIBOR from the earlier cap of LIBOR plus 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4l01ku8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
