\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee rallies off new low on cbank jawboning. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2001\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, April 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit a new low against the dollar on Tuesday before rebounding after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not as overvalued as estimated by the market. \par \par \uc2  By midday the rupee was quoted at 46.94/97 per dollar after it slid to a record intra-day low of 47.10 in early trade - taking losses to over one percent in the past week. It closed at 47.00/02 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was unable to hold ground above 47 rupees as exporters hedged future receipts, state-run banks maintained a steady supply of dollars and banks which are known custodians to offshore funds joined in selling the greenback. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said current market estimates of the rupee's overvaluation against its trade-weighted index, the real effective exchange rate (REER), may not have factored recent falls in the country's inflation rate. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the comments helped firm the rupee's direction in a market waiting for a signal from authorities. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Yashwant Sinha's commment on Monday that the rupee's fall should be viewed in the context of global dollar strength did little to remove the uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "I think the 46.90-47.10 range is the right level for the rupee now...it has depreciated one percent in a week," said V. Ravikumar, head of treasury at Vysya Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The market had been waiting for a comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...and the price action from state-run banks this morning also indicates the slide will be checked here," he said. \par \par \uc2  State-run banks have often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) in the past. \par \par \uc2  OVERVALUED \par \par \uc2  The depreciation started when a foreign fund bought dollars last Tuesday, sparking concerns foreign investors may withdraw from the plunging, scandal-ridden stock market. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Bombay share index has fallen about 27 percent from its high on March 1. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be averse to a fall in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the rupee was nearly three percent overvalued following recent falls in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But on Tuesday, the RBI official told Reuters the market may be overestimating the rupee's appreciation against the REER and reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance that the trade-weighted index is more a medium-term reference for the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "...the level of REER perceived by the market right now does not seem to be reflecting the fall in India's inflation level by about two percent in the last fortnight of March 2001," the official said. \par \par \uc2  India's year-on-year inflation rate, measured by the wholesale price index, fell to 4.87 percent in the week ended March 31 from 6.5 percent in the week ended March 17. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts were quick to point out the actual wholesale price index used in computing the REER has remained steady between 158.4 and 159.2 over the past four months, and only the year-on-year growth levels have dropped. \par \par \uc2  M.R. Madhavan, head of research at Bank of America, said the rupee was still one to two percent overvalued. \par \par \uc2  "The reason the extent of overvaluation is now lower is that the rupee has depreciated one percent in the past week and the Japanese yen has recovered a bit," Madhavan said. \par \par \uc2  "But the euro remains weak, and from the inflation point of view there has been little change," he said. \par \par \uc2  MORE WEAKNESS LATER \par \par \uc2  The depreciation may be contained for now, but traders said the rupee may weaken later in the year and risks for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come from rising crude oil prices, lower demand for exports and a possible decline in foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  There is also political risk over an arms bribery scandal that paralysed parliament on Tuesday. Parliament, which reopened on Monday after a three-week recess, was crippled by an opposition uproar over the scandal for eight days last month before the break. \par \par \uc2  Vasan Shridharan, regional economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's priority will be managing the massive 1.19 trillion rupees government borrowing for 2001/02 (April-March) which has just begun. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI has to ensure the spot rupee weakness does not propagate across the forward curve and push up rates," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4h01tts\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
