\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee - Factors to watch - Sept 19. \b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 05:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to open weak and is likely to test its all time low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  46.08, as demand for dollars from corporates and banks \par \par \uc2  continue, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      - Concerns about an adverse impact on India's finances, due \par \par \uc2  to the rising oil import bill, will weigh and cloud sentiment \par \par \uc2  for the rupee \par \par \uc2      - But comments from a senior monetary official that Indian \par \par \uc2  officials were discussing plans for an overseas bond issue to \par \par \uc2  increase dollar supplies is likely to prop sentiment for the \par \par \uc2  rupee \par \par \uc2      - The official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was working on a \par \par \uc2  three-month schedule to ease the debt burden of oil companies \par \par \uc2  and build the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves -- which are nearly $3 \par \par \uc2  billion lower from their mid-April peak of $38.341 billion. \par \par \uc2      - He added the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) was unlikely to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars or tighten monetary policy at this \par \par \uc2  stage to ward off pressure on the rupee. \par \par \uc2      - The RBI was also not in favour of scrapping the Exchange \par \par \uc2  Earners Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currenct\b0 \highlight\uc2  (EEFC) which was halved last month to \par \par \uc2  increase dollar supplies. \par \par \uc2      - The rupee ended Monday at a record low of 45.99/46.01 to \par \par \uc2  a dollar compared to Friday's close of 45.7750/78. \par \par \uc2      - The Indian unit has so far lost nearly one percent \par \par \uc2  against the dollar in the past week as is barely away from its \par \par \uc2  all time record low of 46.08 on August 11. \par \par \uc2      - A weak stock market was compunding worries about dollar \par \par \uc2  supplies and dealers hope foreign fund buying in equities \par \par \uc2  remain. \par \par \uc2      - Although foreign funds sold equities for a net $47.2 \par \par \uc2  million worth on Thursday and $3.4 million Friday their net \par \par \uc2  purchases in September was $121.9 million. \par \par \uc2      - Bombay shares ended over four percent lower at one-month \par \par \uc2  lows as concerns over high global oil prices combined with an \par \par \uc2  overnight two percent drop in the Nasdaq market sparked off \par \par \uc2  selling by speculators. \par \par \uc2      - Some dollar demand from government agencies to service \par \par \uc2  their debt obligations will also weigh on the rupee. \par \par \uc2      - The one-month forward premia ended at 5.88 percent \par \par \uc2  compared to Friday's close of 5.34 percent. \par \par \uc2       Previous closing rates: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Call money rates\tab \tab   : 7.90-8.25 percent\par   BSE 30-share Index\tab \tab : 4,366.41 (-4.30 pct on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indicators: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves (Sept 8)  : $35.355 bln (-$264\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mln on week) Inflation - wholesale prices (Sept 2)  : 5.64 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yr-on-yr M3 Money supply growth (Aug 25)\tab   : 14.1 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yr-on-yr Industrial production (April-July)     : 5.4 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yr-on-yr Rupee's intra-day low    : 46.08 hit on August 11,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00000