\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Pakistan defends rupee, watching  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Saeed Azhar \par \uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2000\par 12:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KARACHI, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Pakistan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the market on Tuesday, selling dollars to prop up the local rupee against the dollar in what analysts saw as an effort to match moves by India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the State (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Pakistan sought to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaching the 55 mark against the dollar in the interbank market for the second consecutive day. \par \par \uc2  The Pakistani rupee , convertible on the current account, clawed back to 54.57/54.67 in afternoon trade from 55 earlier in the day. The latest level was a 5.3 percent depreciation against the dollar since January. \par \par \uc2  "Basically they are following the Indian rupee. After today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  you've almost matched the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mansoor Ali, research head at brokerage firm Jahangir Siddiqui & Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee was at 45.68/45.69 in afternoon trade, down almost five percent against the dollar since January, but off early August lows that saw it 5.6 percent below the January levels. \par \par \uc2  In the kerb market, the Pakistan rupee was 57.05/57.20 to the dollar in afternoon trade against Monday's close of 57.15/57.25. \par \par \uc2  FIRST TIME \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time ever also sold some dollars for forward transactions in the three-month period to speed up repatriation of delayed export proceeds. \par \par \uc2  "The three-month rate has come down from a high of 56.10 rupees (to a dollar) to 55.35. This will hit exporters hard," said a treasury dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected dollars in a much larger quantity than on Monday, although no exact figures were available. \par \par \uc2  Exporters have withheld around $300 million in the hope of cashing in on a weaker local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to match Pakistan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves with India's because the two countries were competing in exports of mainly cotton-based textile products. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market this year on July 27, 10 days after lifting an unofficial trading band for more than a year that had kept the rupee stable against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The band was eased in May and finally lifted in July. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said Pakistan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  woes, compounded by the absence of multilateral funding due to the suspension of an International Monetary Fund (IMF) programme in mid-1999, were also playing a key role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening. \par \par \uc2  Pakistan recorded a trade deficit of $1.77 billion in the fiscal year that ended in June and has annual debt payments of $2.6 billion, which is 40 percent lower than before 1998 when the country rescheduled payments on its bilateral debt. But that rescheduling period ends in December. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8m0amyp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
