\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee extends losses, awaits RBI moves. \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2000\par 06:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slid to a new intra-day low of 46.08 per dollar in volatile morning trade on Friday on import-driven demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. Volumes were moderate and trade volatile with the rupee swinging between its lifetime low and 45.90, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "State-run banks are there, but they are quoting with the market," said a dealer with a private bank. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders say some state-run banks often act on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it does not want to be seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI wants to keep the surprise element intact and has been maintaining a low profile after making the statement on the rupee in early August," said a treasurer at a private bank. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 46.03/06 per dollar at 10:00 a.m. (0430 GMT) after opening to wide quotes of 45.85/90. It ended at 45.86/87 to a dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums were likely to be volatile, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They will open with a gap and will track the weak spot rate. Traders will also wait for the repo results for further direction later in the day," the private bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The one-month annualised premium ended Thursday at 6.38 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8b0bgxo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
