\par\par \b \uc2  India says balance of payments level comfortable. \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2000\par 10:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, July 13 (Reuters) - India's balance of payments position is comfortable despite a recent fall in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a finance ministry official said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The outlook on the balance of payments remains reasonably good, exports are doing well," Shankar Acharya, the ministry's chief economic adviser told reporters. \par \par \uc2  He was responding to a question on whether recent depletions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were a cause for concern. \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $36.73 billion on June 30, some $1.6 billion down from a peak of $38.34 billion in mid-April. Reserves fell for 10 weeks in a row until June 23 before gaining again the following week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders attributed the fall to a surge in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's oil import bill and to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupee when it was under pressure earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  The rupee fell to a record low of 44.95 per dollar on June 8 before recovering on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since then it has been trading in a 44.64-44.70 per dollar range. \par \par \uc2  "There is no concern that the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will be hit by rising oil prices. Reserves are meant to be used," Acharya said. \par \par \uc2  India's oil import bill more than doubled to $2.63 billion in April-May from the same period a year earlier due to spiralling global oil prices. \par \par \uc2  "Probably by the end of the year, we won't see any significant change in reserves. A drop of $1-2 billion in my opinion is not something to worry about," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((New Delhi Newsroom +91-11-3012024; fax 91-11-3014043; giri.venkatesan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7d01pgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
