\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee seen with firm bias, liquidity weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2000\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, June 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade in a firmer range as tight liquidity conditions in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  money market dissuade traders from holding long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2      * Corporate demand for dollars has eased and dealers said a \par \par \uc2  strengthening rupee could lead to additional dollar supplies \par \par \uc2  from exporters. \par \par \uc2      * Call money rates ended at 13.5-15.0 percent against \par \par \uc2  Saturday's close of 10.0-12.0 percent. \par \par \uc2      * The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) set a cut-off rate of \par \par \uc2  13.5 percent at its one-day reverse repos auction on Monday and \par \par \uc2  dealers said this was a signal the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to keep \par \par \uc2  liquidity tight. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers said higher call money rates made it costly for \par \par \uc2  banks to hold long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      * State-run banks are likely to absorb excess dollar \par \par \uc2  inflows into the market and ensure the rupee does not firm too \par \par \uc2  much. \par \par \uc2      * But the rupee has been firming in the past one week after \par \par \uc2  state-run banks, especially the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  , \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 44.78. \par \par \uc2  * The rupee ended firm at 44.65/66 per dollar against Friday's \par \par \uc2  close of 44.695/705. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers said premia to stay ranged eyeing the tightness \par \par \uc2  in the money market \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended at an annualised 3.36 percent \par \par \uc2  against Friday's close of 3.43 percent. \par \par \uc2      . \par \par \uc2    Previous closing rates: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Call money rates\tab \tab   : 13.50-15.0\par   BSE 30-share Index\tab \tab : 4,837.24 (+72.57)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nasdaq Composite Index: 3,989.83 (+129.27)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dow Jones Indust. Avg : 10,557.84 (+108.54)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indicators:\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves (June 9): $36.855 bln (-0.214)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inflation-wholesale prices(June 3): 6.43 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par M3 Money supply growth (May 19): 15.1 pct yr-on-yr\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rupee's intra-day low: 44.95 on Jun 8, 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6k039pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
