\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee supported amid early light dlr bids. \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2000\par 05:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, June 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opened steady and settled into a narrow range on Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  morning with state-run banks continuing their supply of \par \par \uc2  dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The rupee was quoted at 44.77/785 per dollar at 9:10 a.m. \par \par \uc2  (0340 GMT). \par \par \uc2      It ended at 44.7775/78 on Monday, little changed from \par \par \uc2  Friday's 44.76/78. \par \par \uc2      "The market is still slightly biddish (for dollars), though \par \par \uc2  the SBI is there at the 44.78 level. Corporate interest to \par \par \uc2  hedge July and August payables is strong and if the SBI keeps \par \par \uc2  off, the rupee will weaken," a dealer with a state-run bank \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The State Bank of India's (SBI) dollar supplies at \par \par \uc2  44.78 ensured the rupee did not weaken despite import demand on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the strong support for the rupee at the 44.78 \par \par \uc2  level indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not willing to let it \par \par \uc2  weaken further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has lost over 2.5 percent since early May. The \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally last week when \par \par \uc2  the rupee fell to intra-day lows of 44.95. \par \par \uc2  The pressure on forward premia will remain amid higher call \par \par \uc2  money rates and firm cut-offs at the RBI's reverse repo \par \par \uc2  auctions, both raising concerns short-term liquidity was being \par \par \uc2  tightened to ward off a threat on the rupee, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The six-month premium ended at an annualised 3.23 percent \par \par \uc2  on Monday, compared with the previous day's 3.10 percent. \par \par \uc2      In overseas markets, crude oil prices in the United States \par \par \uc2  rose sharply to hit $31.74 per barrel. \par \par \uc2      The six-month non-deliverable forward dollar was steady at \par \par \uc2  last week's levels of 45.82 rupees. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  Indicators: \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves (June 2): $37.069 bln (-0.255) \par \par \uc2  Inflation-wholesale prices(May 27): 6.59 pct yr-on-yr \par \par \uc2    M3 Money supply growth (May 19)    : 15.1 pct yr-on-yr \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Rupee's intra-day low\tab \tab   : 44.95 on Jun 8, 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6d03q98\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
