\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee weakness to persist,import demand seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2000\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, June 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open steady and weaken slightly in early deals, continuing a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  trend that it has been following over the past few days, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * The market is still uncertain about the levels the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is targeting, at which they expect aggressive \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      * State-run banks' dollar purchases on Monday have given \par \par \uc2  rise to concerns the RBI may be comfortable with the rupee's \par \par \uc2  testing lower levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * Import demand is sustained and rupee's weakness leading \par \par \uc2  to more cautious hedging, thereby pressuring forward premia, \par \par \uc2  they said. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee hit successive closing lows last week, and \par \par \uc2  dealers expect it will inch towards intra-day record lows of \par \par \uc2  44.75 per dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * The State Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (SBI)\tab     has been\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the rupee, but dealers feel it is just\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ensuring the slide is gradual and not too volatile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on May 25 when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupee fell to its weakest level of 44.75, warning the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market against speculation and imposing some measures to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contain volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It also said that it will sell dollars through the SBI to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meet \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs towards oil imports and some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government debt payments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * The rupee closed at 44.665/6725 on Monday, its weakest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close and compared with the previous day's 44.625/635\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Dealers said forward dollar premia will be bid amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continuing weakness in the rupee and slight uptick in call\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Besides the weak rupee, uncertainty in money markets over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the RBI's new liquidity facility through auction-based repos\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and reverse repos will also weigh.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Call rates are expected to remain above the refinance rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of seven percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * The six-month premium ended at an annualised 2.95 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday, compared with the previous day's 2.62 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Previous closing rates:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Call money rates\tab \tab   : 7.25-7.50\par   BSE 30-share Index\tab \tab : 4,531.53 (+78.06)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nasdaq Composite Index: 3,821.76 (+8.38)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dow Jones Indust. Avg : 10,815.30 (+20.54).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indicators:\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves     : $37.324 bln (-0.088)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Inflation (wholesale prices)  : 6.3 pct yr-on-yr (-0.08)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Rupee's intra-day low\tab    : 44.75 on May 25, 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw66046gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
