\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee weak in early deals,cautious dlr bids. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2000\par 05:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, June 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee opened steady on Monday but weakened immediately on dollar purchases by banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market expected import demand, which drove the rupee to successive record closing lows last week, to be sustained. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 44.64/665 per dollar at 9:10 a.m. (0340 GMT). \par \par \uc2  It opened at 44.61/63, little changed from Friday's record closing low of 44.625/635. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were tracking moves of the State Bank of India (SBI), which sold dollars to stem the rupee's slide through last week at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The SBI was moving with the market in opening trade, they said. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on May 25 when the rupee fell to its weakest level of 44.75, warning the market against speculation and imposing some measures to contain volatility. \par \par \uc2  It also said that it will sell dollars through the SBI to meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs towards oil imports and some government debt payments \par \par \uc2  The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen by over a billion dollars from highs of $38.341 billion on April 14. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward dollar premia will be bid amid continuing weakness in the rupee and despite soft call rates. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty in money markets over the RBI's new liquidity facility through auction-based repos and reverse repos will also weigh. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium ended at an annualised 2.62 percent on Friday, compared with the previous day's 2.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw650497j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
