\par\par \b \uc2  Indian short tenor bonds dip, weak rupee weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, June 2 (Reuters) - Indian government bonds extended losses in Friday morning deals on worries over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening rupee supplies in the money market to curb volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) to announce a short or medium term bond auction soon and this had hit buying sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Short and medium tenor bonds fell 5-7 paise (0.05-0.07 rupees), while long dated bonds were flat in a dull trade. \par \par \uc2  The 11.55 percent 2001 bond was down at 102.00 rupees compared to Thursday evening's 102.05 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The 11.85 percent 2001 bond was at 101.40 rupees compared to 101.45 rupees on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The 12.50 percent 2004 bond was dropped to 108.27 rupees from Thursday's 108.34 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rupee's weakness weighed on prices. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term bonds will remain subdued as long as the rupee contiues to weaken," a dealer at a brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, after holding steady around 44.55/57 per dollar for the last three days, slipped on Friday amid persistent demand from corporates. \par \par \uc2  The State Bank of India (SBI), which had protected the rupee from slipping past the 44.60 mark on Thursday, was quoting at current levels. \par \par \uc2  A private bank dealer said the market was uncertain about the direction of bond prices and were waiting for clear signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the rupee movement. \par \par \uc2  Last week the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee fell to its weakest level of 44.75, and warned against speculation and imposed fresh measures to contain volatility. \par \par \uc2  Forward premia rose amid paying pressure from importers after the spot rupee weakened. \par \par \uc2  The six month forward premium annualised was at 2.62 percent compared to the previous close of 2.50 percent. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, anurag.sood@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6204epr\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (india near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\b